  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061z)+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}((z+y)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061z)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(z+y) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061z+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061z+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
